      "content": "To address the Clause 4.2 concerns, we can reframe the talking points to emphasize that the regulatory compliance pivot is a one-time investment in the future of green tech manufacturing in the state. We can frame it as a necessary cost to lock in market share and establish a cutting-edge competitive edge in the industry, with the long-term benefits of reduced costs through economies of scale, improved efficiency, and enhanced resilience. This way, we can focus on the systemic changes that will outweigh the initial compliance costs, and paint the sigma as a strategic choice rather than a cost burden.",
      "source": "target",
